WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.340
{Chapter 06}

00:05.530 --> 00:08.149
You mean a game?

00:08.150 --> 00:09.239
Yes.

00:09.240 --> 00:10.780
We're doing it again.

00:11.620 --> 00:12.620
That okay?

00:13.330 --> 00:18.869
I need to settle the score with you, or I
won't be able to graduate junior-high baseball.

00:18.870 --> 00:21.709
I won't lose to anyone.

00:21.710 --> 00:23.880
That's why we'll play.

00:24.250 --> 00:27.129
But you'd better be in your best form.

00:27.130 --> 00:29.589
I won't accept a repeat of last time.

00:29.590 --> 00:30.640
Okay.

00:31.510 --> 00:32.600
Bro!

00:34.310 --> 00:35.510
Gou's here!

00:39.940 --> 00:40.940
Yo!

00:43.190 --> 00:44.439
Let's play!

00:44.440 --> 00:45.150
What?

00:45.440 --> 00:47.319
We made a promise to Gou and everyone.

00:47.320 --> 00:49.319
I can pitch, can't I?

00:49.320 --> 00:50.819
What are you talking about?

00:50.820 --> 00:54.449
Well, now. Is this the
princess' little brother?

00:54.450 --> 00:55.699
He's so cute!

00:55.700 --> 00:56.909
Do you wanna play with us?

00:56.910 --> 00:57.910
Huh?

00:57.911 --> 00:59.709
C'mon, join us!

00:59.710 --> 01:01.790
Do you wanna play too, mister?

01:03.830 --> 01:06.300
Mister? Are you talking to me?

01:08.130 --> 01:10.299
He called you mister!

01:10.300 --> 01:11.300
Stop laughing, Shun!

01:12.590 --> 01:13.590
Takumi...

01:15.550 --> 01:16.720
You...

01:18.600 --> 01:19.979
Gou, catch for me, okay?

01:19.980 --> 01:21.020
Seiha?

01:21.440 --> 01:23.269
Remember? You promised!

01:23.270 --> 01:25.940
You said you'd catch if I pitched!

01:26.400 --> 01:27.400
Okay.

01:28.190 --> 01:30.189
That mister said he'd play too.

01:30.190 --> 01:31.649
Hold on there, Shorty.

01:31.650 --> 01:33.199
Give me a break, will ya?

01:33.200 --> 01:36.489
I'm only two years older than your brother.

01:36.490 --> 01:37.450
Seriously?

01:37.451 --> 01:40.000
The princess' little
brother doesn't disappoint!

01:40.960 --> 01:43.369
I'll play first base.

01:43.370 --> 01:45.710
Harada, why don't you go
somewhere in the outfield?

01:49.300 --> 01:52.840
Takumi, have you ever
just played baseball for fun?

01:56.010 --> 01:57.010
Don't think so.

02:15.070 --> 02:20.620
I've heard it said so many times

02:21.330 --> 02:27.540
How it's not going to work out

02:28.500 --> 02:34.010
That nothing will change

02:34.340 --> 02:40.510
Even if I pretended not to listen

02:40.970 --> 02:44.349
I knew it all

02:44.350 --> 02:47.519
I learned this from you

02:47.520 --> 02:55.520
That it's not a failure, even when it is

02:56.910 --> 03:03.499
When I thrust my feelings
on to the drifting clouds

03:03.500 --> 03:10.419
The quiet melodies push me forward

03:10.420 --> 03:16.929
Because the sky is so vast and free

03:16.930 --> 03:24.560
I decided that I wouldn't cry anymore

03:34.940 --> 03:37.359
You'd better be ready, Kurinosuke!

03:37.360 --> 03:39.820
You've got a line drive coming your way!

03:40.660 --> 03:41.580
Bring it!

03:41.581 --> 03:43.910
Shun, don't take this so seriously.

03:45.330 --> 03:46.370
Ready?

03:52.380 --> 03:54.340
Good one, Harada's little brother!

03:59.180 --> 04:00.389
All right!

04:00.390 --> 04:01.429
That's an out.

04:01.430 --> 04:04.599
We call that a fly ball, Mizugaki.

04:04.600 --> 04:08.889
Oh my god, why is this
Kurinosuke dude so annoying?!

04:08.890 --> 04:11.940
What is Kaionji teaching these kids?!

04:09.810 --> 04:10.810
Like this.

04:11.940 --> 04:14.279
Stop it with the crocodile tears. Jeez.

04:14.280 --> 04:16.400
He's not bad, though.

04:16.690 --> 04:17.989
You talking about Kurinosuke?

04:17.990 --> 04:19.949
No, the little shorty.

04:19.950 --> 04:22.660
He's throwing the ball nice and low.

04:28.870 --> 04:32.669
Nagakura, you need to work on
your form when you catch pop-ups.

04:32.670 --> 04:34.499
You have to look more graceful.

04:34.500 --> 04:35.549
Yeah, yeah.

04:35.550 --> 04:37.799
Please teach me when
we get back to practice.

04:37.800 --> 04:40.299
What? Please teach you?

04:40.300 --> 04:42.050
Are you playing catcher again?

04:45.510 --> 04:46.679
All right.

04:46.680 --> 04:48.429
I'm up.

04:48.430 --> 04:50.690
You can do it, mister!

04:52.940 --> 04:54.319
Seiha.

04:54.320 --> 04:56.940
Be sure you grip the center of the ball.

05:00.200 --> 05:02.199
You can do it, mister!

05:02.200 --> 05:03.569
Shut up, Shun.

05:03.570 --> 05:05.449
That was Kurinosuke, not me!

05:05.450 --> 05:07.450
You're both the same. All right, listen up.

05:08.000 --> 05:11.079
I'll show you how to
hit a low and slow pitch.

05:11.080 --> 05:12.210
Okay!

05:18.340 --> 05:19.340
Get it, Takumi!

05:28.350 --> 05:29.679
Out!

05:29.680 --> 05:30.849
Yeah!

05:30.850 --> 05:32.689
Too bad.

05:32.690 --> 05:34.939
No way. I was totally safe.

05:34.940 --> 05:36.689
Oh, Shuugo.

05:36.690 --> 05:40.439
Your sliding is so bad because
you're so used to hitting homers.

05:40.440 --> 05:42.949
I should've made it with that hit.

05:42.950 --> 05:45.199
I can't believe they stopped me.

05:45.200 --> 05:48.409
The princess is no joke.

05:48.410 --> 05:51.040
Beating him is gonna be so sweet.

05:51.710 --> 05:52.829
Nagakura.

05:52.830 --> 05:53.999
Yes?

05:54.000 --> 05:56.709
You'd better have Harada ready by spring.

05:56.710 --> 05:59.760
Make sure you get him in his top condition.

06:00.340 --> 06:03.929
Then I'm gonna make him cry on that mound.

06:03.930 --> 06:05.679
Remember that.

06:05.680 --> 06:07.349
I don't think it's possible.

06:07.350 --> 06:08.350
Huh?

06:09.220 --> 06:10.600
To defeat Takumi.

06:11.390 --> 06:13.100
To make him cry on the mound.

06:13.810 --> 06:15.600
I don't think anybody could do that.

06:17.360 --> 06:21.989
Jeez, you're worse than Shuugo.

06:21.990 --> 06:23.569
Whatever.

06:23.570 --> 06:25.860
Just be ready.

06:28.240 --> 06:30.659
See! I pitched well, didn't I?

06:30.660 --> 06:31.660
Yeah.

06:34.960 --> 06:36.630
That was a good throw.

06:38.790 --> 06:39.790
Yeah.

06:44.170 --> 06:45.170
Takumi...

06:47.640 --> 06:48.850
I...

07:22.920 --> 07:23.959
Good morning.

07:23.960 --> 07:24.960
Morning.

07:28.300 --> 07:29.889
It's snowing.

07:29.890 --> 07:32.510
Came early this year.

07:47.780 --> 07:50.779
Gou has to be Harada's
catcher. It can't be anyone else.

07:50.780 --> 07:51.780
I'm so glad.

07:52.200 --> 07:56.039
You say the same thing every day.

07:56.040 --> 07:57.409
You've gotta stop.

07:57.410 --> 08:00.209
Well, it's what I really think.

08:00.210 --> 08:01.669
You're with me, right, Higashi?

08:01.670 --> 08:03.589
Sawa's right.

08:03.590 --> 08:07.629
He had me worried for a
second, but Gou pulled through.

08:07.630 --> 08:10.549
He knows exactly what he needs to do.

08:10.550 --> 08:15.349
Now that Nitta East's battery is
back together, let's get cracking!

08:15.350 --> 08:21.979
You know, you two should worry more about
getting a starter's spot than our battery.

08:21.980 --> 08:26.069
I'm so busy with all the practice I
have to do as the starting third baseman.

08:26.070 --> 08:27.989
Who's a starter now?

08:27.990 --> 08:29.529
Stop making things up.

08:29.530 --> 08:31.819
Are you stupid? Everyone's saying it.

08:31.820 --> 08:35.739
That the genius Yoshisada
is the best man for third base.

08:35.740 --> 08:37.960
Nobody says that!

08:44.550 --> 08:47.460
I don't want to grow older.

08:47.840 --> 08:50.629
You shouldn't be saying
that until you hit twenty.

08:50.630 --> 08:57.470
But we'll be seniors next summer, which means we'll
have to quit baseball and focus on studying for exams.

08:57.810 --> 08:58.929
I really don't want that.

08:58.930 --> 09:01.480
I wish I could play baseball forever.

09:03.480 --> 09:06.109
Then do it. You can play in high school.

09:06.110 --> 09:08.359
But we're having fun right...

09:08.360 --> 09:09.570
Ow!

09:09.571 --> 09:10.900
You're way too inflexible.

09:10.900 --> 09:12.240
Spread your legs more.

09:10.901 --> 09:12.990
Ouch!

09:13.410 --> 09:14.410
Takumi.

09:16.200 --> 09:17.699
The captain wants you.

09:17.700 --> 09:18.700
Let's go.

09:22.250 --> 09:23.379
Yo.

09:23.380 --> 09:25.499
It feels like it's been a long time.

09:25.500 --> 09:26.879
Kaionji!

09:26.880 --> 09:28.419
You finished your exams?

09:28.420 --> 09:29.839
Finally.

09:29.840 --> 09:31.509
So, Nonomura.

09:31.510 --> 09:33.799
Could I borrow these two for a second?

09:33.800 --> 09:35.009
Of course.

09:35.010 --> 09:37.850
I'll go lead our next drills.

09:38.930 --> 09:39.979
Gather up!

09:39.980 --> 09:42.140
He's really settling in as captain.

09:40.350 --> 09:41.480
Okay!

09:42.520 --> 09:43.939
He was a good choice.

09:43.940 --> 09:44.940
Yes.

09:45.560 --> 09:48.649
Keep the last Sunday in March free.

09:48.650 --> 09:50.649
Does that mean what I think it means?

09:50.650 --> 09:51.450
Yeah.

09:51.451 --> 09:53.030
Our game with Yokote.

09:53.780 --> 09:57.660
We might've graduated already, but
we'll go with the same members as before.

09:59.120 --> 10:01.410
That won't be a problem, will it?

10:02.000 --> 10:04.630
We won't crumble like we did before.

10:05.540 --> 10:07.170
Please tell them that.

10:07.880 --> 10:10.380
You guys better not back down.

10:11.510 --> 10:13.630
Sorry for interrupting your practice.

10:14.430 --> 10:15.679
Kaionji.

10:15.680 --> 10:16.550
Yes, sir.

10:16.551 --> 10:19.179
You wanna get in the batter's box?

10:19.180 --> 10:20.180
What?

10:20.680 --> 10:22.599
I mean, you've come all this way.

10:22.600 --> 10:25.939
I figured you'd want to feel
what it's like to hit the ball again.

10:25.940 --> 10:29.819
But I haven't practiced
for real in a while.

10:29.820 --> 10:31.359
I know you.

10:31.360 --> 10:34.319
I'm sure you at least
swung a bat every day.

10:34.320 --> 10:35.320
Yes, sir.

10:35.530 --> 10:37.739
I'll let you hit a real ball.

10:37.740 --> 10:39.080
It'll wake you up.

10:46.040 --> 10:47.079
Are you ready?

10:47.080 --> 10:48.250
Yes.

11:05.230 --> 11:07.229
That's enough, Nagakura.

11:07.230 --> 11:08.770
I'm ready now.

11:09.060 --> 11:11.110
Get ready, Kaionji.

11:29.170 --> 11:32.800
He's not throwing balls on purpose, is he?

11:35.300 --> 11:37.549
Then why isn't he hitting the strike zone?

11:37.550 --> 11:39.510
Are you in the right position?

11:52.230 --> 11:53.230
Takumi.

12:12.880 --> 12:14.550
Thank you very much!

12:17.050 --> 12:22.349
Nonomura, why don't we give all the
starters a chance to hit off of Harada?

12:22.350 --> 12:23.350
Yes, sir.

12:25.180 --> 12:26.390
Right side!

12:28.020 --> 12:30.809
What was that, Coach?

12:30.810 --> 12:32.979
You mean Harada or Nagakura?

12:32.980 --> 12:34.569
Both of them.

12:34.570 --> 12:36.570
The way Harada's pitches were veering...

12:37.490 --> 12:39.819
I thought there was a chance.

12:39.820 --> 12:42.619
Getting you in the batter's box...

12:42.620 --> 12:45.079
Turns out he's pretty simple to understand.

12:45.080 --> 12:47.159
What are you talking about?

12:47.160 --> 12:52.079
How can someone who was so good at ball
control not be able to throw strikes now?

12:52.080 --> 12:53.089
Besides...

12:53.090 --> 12:58.090
Just when you think a strike is coming,
it packs a real punch.

12:58.420 --> 13:01.340
Anybody would struggle to hit that.

13:02.550 --> 13:04.719
And Nagakura was acting strange too.

13:04.720 --> 13:08.599
Wouldn't you normally go talk to the pitcher
if they kept missing the strike zone?

13:08.600 --> 13:12.019
I actually talked to Nonomura about this.

13:12.020 --> 13:15.399
I told him I'd get you in the
batter's box if you turned up.

13:15.400 --> 13:19.529
I wanted to see whether or not
that battery could actually be used.

13:19.530 --> 13:20.900
What do you mean?

13:21.570 --> 13:23.989
You know that Nagakura
had a moment of doubt, right?

13:23.990 --> 13:24.740
Yes.

13:24.741 --> 13:30.620
Yet when practice started up again after
finals, he took up the mitt and got all set up.

13:31.580 --> 13:34.419
I mean, at first, I was
thinking it was about time.

13:34.420 --> 13:37.629
But then something with Harada was wrong.

13:37.630 --> 13:39.670
You mean the veering?

13:40.340 --> 13:43.339
I was honestly surprised too.

13:43.340 --> 13:47.640
Harada couldn't control his own pitches?

13:47.930 --> 13:50.229
I mean, they're not all bad.

13:50.230 --> 13:52.439
Sometimes he gets some good ones in.

13:52.440 --> 13:53.979
And his pitches...

13:53.980 --> 13:57.649
His pitches are stronger than
anything he's thrown before, right?

13:57.650 --> 13:58.650
Yeah.

13:58.980 --> 14:03.659
In other words, Harada and
Nagakura aren't doing well as a battery.

14:03.660 --> 14:05.409
Is that what it means?

14:05.410 --> 14:06.739
I suppose so.

14:06.740 --> 14:08.659
What could be the cause?

14:08.660 --> 14:09.829
I don't have a clue.

14:09.830 --> 14:13.079
That's why I put you in the batter's box.

14:13.080 --> 14:14.959
So how are they?

14:14.960 --> 14:16.749
What's different about them?

14:16.750 --> 14:18.549
Tell me what you're thinking.

14:18.550 --> 14:21.879
Has this really been
giving you trouble, sir?

14:21.880 --> 14:23.429
Of course.

14:23.430 --> 14:27.099
Forget Nagakura, where
else am I going to put Harada?

14:27.100 --> 14:30.639
He's only got value on the mound.

14:30.640 --> 14:32.560
It'd be a waste not to use him.

14:37.110 --> 14:41.689
Maybe he hasn't been able to
get his pitches under control yet.

14:41.690 --> 14:48.829
You're saying that his pitches suddenly got so
strong that even he can't get them under control yet?

14:48.830 --> 14:50.040
I'm just guessing.

14:50.990 --> 14:54.159
Kaionji, you're really something.

14:54.160 --> 14:56.330
I just stood there in the batter's box.

14:57.040 --> 14:59.960
They're the ones who are amazing.

15:00.460 --> 15:03.470
He's the one who drew
out Harada's potential.

15:04.300 --> 15:08.300
Harada's able to throw all-out
because Nagakura is his catcher.

15:26.530 --> 15:27.570
Kadowaki.

15:29.120 --> 15:31.579
Yo, Kaionji. Long time no see.

15:31.580 --> 15:33.290
I keep telling you.

15:33.580 --> 15:36.789
Stop hanging the towel around your neck.
You look like an old man.

15:36.790 --> 15:38.039
Who cares?

15:38.040 --> 15:39.629
What are you two doing together?

15:39.630 --> 15:42.379
Kaionji kept pestering me about a date.

15:42.380 --> 15:43.959
So we went and had lunch.

15:43.960 --> 15:47.009
You could've called me too.

15:47.010 --> 15:49.549
Instead, you texted me to
meet you here immediately.

15:49.550 --> 15:54.310
It's just something that might've
been too much for you to handle.

15:54.810 --> 15:57.559
What do you mean by that?

15:57.560 --> 15:59.729
You really don't want to know.

15:59.730 --> 16:03.069
You might get a heart
attack from your jealousy.

16:03.070 --> 16:07.070
Isn't there any better way you
could bring this up with him?

16:07.610 --> 16:12.950
I just said that I got to experience
Harada's pitches from the batter's box again.

16:14.450 --> 16:17.079
He said he can't throw strikes.

16:17.080 --> 16:19.459
Who can't throw strikes?

16:19.460 --> 16:21.839
Who do you think we're
talking about right now?

16:21.840 --> 16:24.629
Your princess, obviously.

16:24.630 --> 16:26.090
What do you mean?

16:27.470 --> 16:29.840
I got the chills.

16:30.510 --> 16:35.469
They might not go as far as you,
Kadowaki, but I get my fair share of hits.

16:35.470 --> 16:38.349
I choked up on the bat
and really tried to hit it.

16:38.350 --> 16:40.399
You didn't even graze it?

16:40.400 --> 16:44.019
It wasn't the kind of pitch
I'm ever going to be able to hit.

16:44.020 --> 16:46.569
It just left me feeling frustrated.

16:46.570 --> 16:49.029
Why couldn't I even hit it?

16:49.030 --> 16:51.990
So you just wanted someone to complain to.

16:52.780 --> 16:54.659
Shuugo, go ahead and get mad at him.

16:54.660 --> 16:57.699
He came here just to complain to us.

16:57.700 --> 17:01.079
He thinks we'd understand his frustration.

17:01.080 --> 17:03.379
Could he underestimate us any more?

17:03.380 --> 17:04.589
That's not it.

17:04.590 --> 17:07.459
I honestly thought that Nagakura
and Harada were both amazing.

17:07.460 --> 17:10.880
They were pitching and
catching like it was nothing.

17:11.590 --> 17:16.259
It's hard to admit, but just for a moment,
I felt this hatred for them.

17:16.260 --> 17:17.890
That's the honest truth.

17:25.730 --> 17:27.649
How old are you again?

17:27.650 --> 17:30.399
You're, what, fifteen or sixteen
and still with the self-loathing?

17:30.400 --> 17:32.659
Grow up already.

17:32.660 --> 17:34.659
You and Shuugo are both idiots.

17:34.660 --> 17:36.410
Stop trying to act so cool.

17:38.240 --> 17:39.499
Hey, that's going too far.

17:39.500 --> 17:41.960
If I don't, I can't get it
through to you guys, right?

17:44.000 --> 17:49.800
The princess keeps getting the best of you
because you're always posing as the cool athlete.

17:50.300 --> 17:53.050
You both seem fake.

17:53.390 --> 17:55.849
The princess is a wicked witch.

17:55.850 --> 17:57.640
So go ahead and hate him.

17:58.310 --> 18:02.059
How many times have you
killed him in your dreams already?

18:02.060 --> 18:03.649
I haven't killed him.

18:03.650 --> 18:05.269
Then did you beat him up?

18:05.270 --> 18:08.319
Or was it more of a naughty dream?

18:08.320 --> 18:09.320
Shun!

18:13.530 --> 18:15.779
I'm getting real tired of your mouth!

18:15.780 --> 18:17.119
Wow, you're actually mad.

18:17.120 --> 18:18.539
Is it because I was right?

18:18.540 --> 18:20.619
You really fell for him hard, huh?

18:20.620 --> 18:23.540
Are you making fun of me?!

18:24.460 --> 18:26.540
It pisses me off watching you.

18:27.250 --> 18:28.589
Hey, Shuugo.

18:28.590 --> 18:30.670
Just be honest.

18:30.960 --> 18:32.419
You dreamed about it, right?

18:32.420 --> 18:34.679
Does he strike you out
in your own dreams too?

18:34.680 --> 18:37.760
Are you really that scared of the princess?

18:39.220 --> 18:40.390
Screw you.

18:41.890 --> 18:43.390
Stop it, Kadowaki!

18:45.310 --> 18:48.229
Shuugo, that's assault.

18:48.230 --> 18:53.649
"Yokote's Kadowaki assaulted
and injured a teammate."

18:53.650 --> 18:56.409
Wouldn't that jeopardize your scholarship?

18:56.410 --> 18:57.699
Stop it!

18:57.700 --> 18:59.739
Why are you trying to provoke him?!

18:59.740 --> 19:01.409
What are you trying to say?!

19:01.410 --> 19:02.909
Nothing.

19:02.910 --> 19:07.289
I just thought I'd show you that the
thing you're desperately trying to protect

19:07.290 --> 19:11.420
can all get taken away
with one little fight.

19:11.800 --> 19:13.589
Getting in to a prestigious school.

19:13.590 --> 19:15.759
Doing well at nationals.

19:15.760 --> 19:19.549
Is that all you're working your
ass off in baseball for, idiot?

19:19.550 --> 19:21.389
I never said that!

19:21.390 --> 19:23.559
You didn't have to.

19:23.560 --> 19:27.150
Losing to the princess scares you.

19:27.730 --> 19:30.149
If you lose, your confidence will be shot.

19:30.150 --> 19:32.150
That's what you're scared of, isn't it?

19:34.740 --> 19:37.410
Stop talking like you know anything.

19:38.110 --> 19:42.910
The reason why you can't beat
the princess isn't because he's better.

19:43.410 --> 19:45.959
The princess is still unknown.

19:45.960 --> 19:48.960
There's no expectations or fanfare for him.

19:49.710 --> 19:52.419
He isn't carrying any
baggage like that around.

19:52.420 --> 19:54.879
It's just baseball.

19:54.880 --> 19:58.339
Just enjoy the game, play by play.

19:58.340 --> 20:00.179
That's all there is to it.

20:00.180 --> 20:01.600
Stop it, Kadowaki!

20:03.810 --> 20:06.179
Trying to act cool makes
you look like an idiot.

20:06.180 --> 20:12.230
You're struggling so much because you're playing
the part of the almighty Kadowaki who's never lost.

20:25.790 --> 20:26.790
Shuugo.

20:27.460 --> 20:30.629
Mizugaki! Just stop talking already!

20:30.630 --> 20:32.379
Kadowaki, you should leave!

20:32.380 --> 20:33.750
Kneel.

20:37.920 --> 20:41.340
If you don't want me to
tell anybody that you hit me,

20:41.970 --> 20:44.010
you'll kneel on the ground and apologize.

20:44.720 --> 20:45.600
Mizugaki!

20:45.601 --> 20:50.230
You know, I've always wanted
to make you kneel in front of me.

20:50.690 --> 20:52.520
I've felt that this whole time.

20:52.980 --> 20:56.480
I bet you never even noticed, did you?

21:00.110 --> 21:03.069
I'll tell you one last thing, Shuugo.

21:03.070 --> 21:05.620
The reason why you've
fallen so hard for the princess

21:06.160 --> 21:11.880
is because you think he'll strip away
all that baggage you're carrying around.

21:21.720 --> 21:24.075
Summer's peak came and went

21:26.430 --> 21:32.769
That's what the weather report said

21:32.770 --> 21:39.255
But it still feels like
the city is restless

21:47.120 --> 21:55.120
The evening bells of 5 p.m.
resonate inside my heart today

22:02.050 --> 22:08.450
Clouding me with something
convenient like "destiny"

22:20.421 --> 22:24.109
It's the final fireworks of the year

22:24.110 --> 22:27.825
I will remember them for years to come

22:31.540 --> 22:33.375
Are you here? You're probably not

22:35.210 --> 22:37.105
I'm sure you're not

22:39.000 --> 22:40.815
Will I be able to say it if I see you?

22:42.630 --> 22:45.445
I close my eyes and dream

22:54.910 --> 22:57.579
<i>You were pitching for
batting practice all day.</i>

22:57.580 --> 22:58.620
<i>Why did you hold back?</i>

22:59.710 --> 23:01.960
<i>You don't need to go all-out today?</i>

23:02.540 --> 23:03.840
<i>I can see it on your face.</i>

23:06.470 --> 23:08.010
<i>It's okay, Grandpa.</i>

23:08.550 --> 23:10.970
<i>He's not mad at you.</i>

23:11.760 --> 23:14.220
<i>That was really cool, though.</i>

23:16.520 --> 23:19.730
<i>Didn't you say you wanted to go to Koshien?</i>

23:20.940 --> 23:21.940
<i>A year ago, I did.</i>

23:23.150 --> 23:25.530
<i>But I can't even think about that now.</i>

23:26.190 --> 23:27.360
I'm too tired.

23:27.361 --> 23:29.510
Episode 10: "That Day Again"
